## 4. Setting up GitHub Actions Correctly
If you want to use the GitHub Actions CI/CD workflow you pasted, **do not paste it in the terminal**. 

1. Create a repository on GitHub.
2. In your local codebase, create a folder structure exactly like this:
   `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
3. Paste your YAML configuration into that `deploy.yml` file.
4. Add your Google Cloud Service Account Key to your GitHub Repository Secrets under **`GCP_SA_KEY`**.
5. When you push to your `main` branch, GitHub will automatically log in and deploy your telemetry function for you!